{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e96402222e17ff72","name":"Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-e96402222e17ff72","title":"Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter","revision":18682,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:32:54Z","sha256":"446d57fceb067c9068c30d7a0aadef01e24151adb9cb7cf3a1096438005d1e59","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18682","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Cutlass-9%20Patrol%20Fighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e96402222e17ff72","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During the height of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The SoroSuub Corporation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_SoroSuub_Corporation","referenceId":"reference:98bcb386dd9e3201"}," decided to design and build a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," it could produce, modify, and utilize for its own needs. This patrol fighter was the Cutlass series, the last (and most successful) model of which was the Cutlass-9. Originally intended purely as a corporate asset, the Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter was popular enough to spur some sales to other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", especially nonhumans. As ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}," began to groan under the weight of its own success, many humanocentric companies began treating nonhuman buyers as second-class citizens. SoroSuub never had that attitude, and sold many more Cutlass-9s as a result.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Once ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}," came into power, SoroSuub had to tread a much more careful line. Having supported ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"},", the company had to take extreme measures to prove itself to the Empire. One such step was to stop production of the Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter, which the Empire saw as a ship preferred by malcontents and rebels. By the time SoroSuub underwent an internal revolution and switched to supporting ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},", the rebels needed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," far more than fighters, and no further Cutlass-9s were built. Being sturdy and easily modified vessels, some survived in independant hands, but they became increasingly rare after the end of the Galactic Civil War.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The basic Cutlass-9 was a simple fighter, with two mid-grade lasers and a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missile Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missile_Launcher"},". It had a Class 2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"}," and weak shields, making it a good long-range fighter when it was produced. Because it was always intended to be modified to suit the needs of SoroSuub, it was built with additional unused power conduits (giving it 3 unused ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emplacement Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emplacement_Points"},"). This additional capacity was often used to upgrade the shields or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},", or to add more powerful lasers and missile weapons.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," spurred the development of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", the Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter went from cutting-edge to outdated. It was possible to upgrade it with the unused ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emplacement Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emplacement_Points"},", but few owners bothered.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Cutlass-9 Patrol Fighter Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense